1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
From hunting to a shared camp
Three teams hunt in separate grounds and share one camp.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Three teams hunt
Fast-moving stags need cooperation. Hares can be caught alone.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Dividing the harvest
Hunters divide their food between themselves, their team and the shared camp.

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The camp feeds everyone
Shared food supports the whole society. Some food remains in storage.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
An ecological shock
Stored food is lost. The camp now has less than it needs for the next meal.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
The next hunt
The teams hunt again. Their new harvest creates a new contribution decision.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Giving more to the camp
In this scripted example, every team sends more of its next harvest to the camp.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Recovery through contribution
The camp can feed everyone again and rebuild its reserve.
